# ============================================================================
#  zm_qol — .gitignore
#
#  NOTE: the big binaries ARE tracked on purpose. mod.ff, mod.all.sabl/.sabs and
#  deathmachine_zm.all.sabl have no source in this project and cannot be
#  regenerated from anything here — losing them loses the mod. Same for
#  zone_source/base/mod.ff, the donor fastfile every rebuild links from.
#  A checkpoint you can't actually restore from isn't a checkpoint.
# ============================================================================

# Runtime logs pulled off the game — noise, and regenerated every crash hunt.
crashlogs/

# Linker scratch output; build_ff.bat deletes it, but not if a build failed.
zone_out/
zone_source/_regen/

# Staged copies of the .csc sources, written by build_ff.bat step "Staging current
# .csc sources" so the Linker picks them up instead of the donor's stale originals.
# Pure build artifacts — the real files are scripts/zm/**/*.csc.
zone_assets/scripts/

# Ad-hoc backups made before risky edits.
*.bak-*
*.bak

# Replacement stock soundbanks (Carbon BO2 Sound Remaster), deployed by
# build.bat's %OPTFILES% but NOT tracked: cmn_root.all.sabl is 267 MB, well over
# GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard limit, and unlike mod.all.sabl it is not ours and
# is re-downloadable. A clone without it builds fine and plays stock weapon audio.
# Source: H:\Claude\Carbon Black Ops 2 Sound Remaster\
cmn_root.all.sabl
cmn_root.all.sabs

# Windows/editor cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# Sound Studio working copies. The real banks (mod.all.sabl/.sabs,
# deathmachine_zm.all.sabl) ARE tracked - these are scratch duplicates made
# before an alias import and would just bloat history.
*- Copy.sab*
* - Copy.*

# Sound-bank build inputs, regenerated by build_ff.bat from zone_source\base\.
# The donor's 249 payloads and its 1,691-row alias table both come straight back
# out of base\mod.ff + base\mod.all.sabl, so they are derived, not source.
# What IS source: soundbank\mod.all.aliases.additions.csv and sound\.
zone_assets/soundbank/
zone_assets/sound/

# mod.iwd is no longer tracked. Since the upscaled texture pack landed it is
# ~2.1 GB, and git would store a fresh copy of it on every release commit -
# the repo would pass GitHub's file-size limit within one release. It is a
# BUILD OUTPUT and fully reproducible: build.bat regenerates it from the raw
# folders (images/, scripts/, maps/, weapons/, ui_mp/, ...), all of which ARE
# tracked. Nothing is lost that cannot be rebuilt.
#
# 🛑 The other five shipped files stay tracked on purpose - mod.ff,
# mod.all.sabl, mod.all.sabs and deathmachine_zm.all.sabl have no source in
# this project and CANNOT be regenerated. See CLAUDE.md section 5.
mod.iwd

# The upscaled / BO3-style texture pack (2,852 .iwi, ~2.1 GB) that ships inside
# mod.iwd. NOT tracked: it would add 2.1 GB to a repo that is otherwise ~86 MB,
# and it is not this project's work - the master copy is
#   H:\Claude\Projects Sources\add textures to mod
#
# 🛑 This rule does NOT untrack the mod's own 64 images. gitignore never affects
# files git already tracks, and those 64 were committed long before the pack
# arrived, so they stay in history. Only the new bulk textures are skipped.
#
# 🛑 CONSEQUENCE, so nobody is surprised: a FRESH CLONE cannot rebuild the full
# mod.iwd. It will build fine and play fine, just with stock-resolution textures
# until the pack folder above is copied back into images\.
images/*.iwi

# 🛑 v2.1.3 - EXCEPTIONS, because these two are the MOD'S OWN and it is broken
# without them. They are the stock 64x64 power-up HUD icons for Zombie Blood and
# Fire Sale, whose pixels live in DLC ipaks that are not mounted off their home
# maps - so the icon draws as nothing unless mod.iwd carries the .iwi. See
# zone_source\mod_locations.zone for the measurement. Anything else added here
# must be an asset the mod needs to function, never a texture-pack file.
!images/specialty_zomblood_zombies.iwi
!images/specialty_firesale_zombies.iwi

# 🛑 v2.15.6 - THE L96A1'S TEN IMAGES, same rule as the two above: the mod's own
# assets, and the gun is BROKEN without them. mod.ff carries only the image
# HEADERS (every image in it dumps as "Could not find data" - the pixels always
# ship as .iwi). For a retail gun those pixels come from the player's Black Ops II
# install; the L96A1 is a Black Ops 1 port, so NO retail .iwi exists and nothing
# supplies them but this folder. Shipped without them (v2.15.0-v2.15.5) the gun
# rendered ENTIRELY BLACK and the scope overlay drew nothing at all when aiming
# down sights (user screenshot, Tunnel survival, 2026-09-09).
#
# The other three Black Ops 1 guns need no entry here: their materials name
# t6_wpn_* images that retail Black Ops II already ships, which is why the M60
# and the Browning render correctly while the L96A1 did not.
!images/t5_l96a1_base_c.iwi
!images/t5_l96a1_base_n.iwi
!images/t5_l96a1_base_s.iwi
!images/t5_l96a1_lens_c.iwi
!images/t5_l96a1_lens_s.iwi
!images/t5_l96a1_plastic_c.iwi
!images/t5_l96a1_scope_inner_c.iwi
!images/t5_l96a1_scope_inner_s.iwi
!images/t5_l96a1_scope_overlay.iwi
!images/hud_t5_l96a1.iwi

# 1.9 GB of optional payloads the INSTALLER ships, not the mod: the upscaled
# texture pack for the player's Plutonium images folder and the custom sound
# banks for their zone folder. Far past any sane git limit - they belong in a
# release asset, never in the tree.
Optionals/

# The installer writes its own run log next to itself.
installer/installer.log

# A 1.1 GB zip of Optionals\ - never belongs in git (GitHub rejects >100 MB files).
Optionals.zip

# ============================================================================
#  Development notes and agent state — moved OUT of this folder 2026-08-20 at
#  the user's request, to keep the repo to the mod's own source. They now live
#  in the sibling folder  "Projects Sources\zm_qol - dev\"  and are NOT public:
#      .agents\            checkpoints + QUEUE.md / QUEUE_LIST.md
#      CLAUDE.md           working practice for this project
#      AI_CONTEXT.md       GSC/T6 primer
#      MOD_CATALOGUE.md    every change the mod makes
#      STOCK_REFERENCE.md  vanilla BO2 behaviour reference
#      ERROR_CATALOGUE.md  every error class hit, and its pre-flight check
#      parsed\             gsc-tool parse output (build artifact)
#      crashlogs\          logs pulled off the game
#  🛑 NOTHING in the build reads any of them — verified by grep over every
#  .bat/.ps1/.sh/.zone/.json/.gsc/.csc/.lua before the move: the only hits were
#  GSC *comments* citing them by name. Re-adding them here would republish
#  private notes, so they are ignored as well as gone.
# ============================================================================
.agents/
CLAUDE.md
AI_CONTEXT.md
MOD_CATALOGUE.md
STOCK_REFERENCE.md
ERROR_CATALOGUE.md
parsed/

# The installer's own run log — it records local paths and the user's install
# history. It is written next to qol-installer.ps1, which lives in Mod Files\.
installer/Mod Files/installer.log

# v2.3.2 - build.bat now deploys the 5 built mod files into installer\Mod
# Files\ too (Act-InstallMod copies FROM there, and a stale copy sitting there
# silently reinstalled OLD code over a fresh build - see build.bat's [6/8]).
# They are BUILD OUTPUT, byte-for-byte the same files already tracked at the
# project root, so tracking a second copy here would just double ~115 MB of
# binaries in history for something regenerated on every build.
installer/Mod Files/mod.ff
installer/Mod Files/mod.iwd
installer/Mod Files/mod.json
installer/Mod Files/mod.all.sabl
installer/Mod Files/mod.all.sabs

# ============================================================================
#  v2.2.0 - THE FULL RESHADE SHADER COLLECTION IS NOT TRACKED.
#
#  User request, 2026-08-22: *"install all the shaders from reshade because
#  right now when i installed with the install script for my mod it just
#  installs the shaders that the preset uses."* The installer now ships the
#  whole collection - 856 files, 130 MB, of which 121 MB is the Textures folder
#  (LUTs, blue-noise, dirt masks; pd80_example-lut.png alone is 11 MB).
#
#  🛑 IT IS THIRD-PARTY AND IT IS BULK, so it follows the same rule as
#  Optionals\, images\*.iwi and mod.iwd above: it ships in the RELEASE ASSET,
#  not in the tree. The user asked on 2026-08-20 that this repo carry the mod's
#  own source only, and 130 MB of other people's shaders in the permanent
#  history of a public repo is the opposite of that.
#
#  🛑 CONSEQUENCE, so nobody is surprised: a fresh clone cannot rebuild the
#  release package's ReShade half. The master copy is  H:\Claude\reshade-vault\
#  and the shipped copy is the release zip. Everything else under reshade\ -
#  BO2.ini, ReShade.ini and dxgi.dll - IS still tracked, so the preset and the
#  loader survive a clone.
#
#  📝 The 20 files that were tracked before this (the subset the preset used)
#  are removed from the index in the same commit; they stay in history.
# ============================================================================
installer/Mod Files/reshade/reshade-shaders/

# ============================================================================
#  Desktop shortcuts (.lnk) are machine-local, not source.
#
#  "Quality Of Life BO2.lnk" points at H:\Claude\...\installer\Windows Install.bat
#  with an icon under H:\Customization\ and the authoring machine's name baked
#  into its tracking block. On anyone else's PC it is a dead link, so it belongs
#  on this desktop and not in the repo. The installer's .bat files ARE tracked.
# ============================================================================
*.lnk

# Local VS Code workspace settings — per-machine, not part of the mod.
.vscode/
